<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Hardened-runtime entitlements for the RUST backend build, where the app
  serves itself and no Node process is bundled (Phase 6). Every entitlement
  the Node build needs exists for Node, so this file grants none of them.

  What the Node build grants, and why it is gone here:

  • allow-jit
      V8 JIT-compiles at runtime, which the hardened runtime blocks without
      this. There is no V8 in this build. The webview still JITs, but
      WebKit does that in its own process (com.apple.WebKit.WebContent),
      which Apple ships with its own entitlements; the host app does not
      need them.

  • allow-unsigned-executable-memory
      For the V8 codepaths that write pages codesign would otherwise
      reject. Nothing in this build writes executable memory: the server is
      compiled Rust.

  • allow-dyld-environment-variables
      So the Node helper could find the adjacent .node bindings. This build
      loads no dynamic libraries of its own: SQLite is compiled into the
      binary (rusqlite's bundled build).

  Still deliberately NOT set, as in the Node build:

  • disable-library-validation
      Library validation is what stops a tampered library being loaded into
      a signed process, and nothing here needs it relaxed.

  An empty dict is intentional: it is the strictest thing that can be
  signed, and the release verifier asserts the shipped binary carries no
  entitlement the Node build needed.
-->
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
</dict>
</plist>
